      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the FDA-labeled maximum.\n\n- **Daily total:** The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 1,700 mg is well above the usual maximum of about 850\u20131,000 mg per dose.\n- **Risk:** An overdose raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the standard maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** This could be 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose or formulation.** For example, an extended-release product, which is usually given once daily.\n\nTell me which dose you want. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, confirm that explicitly and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional."
      }
     ],
